    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35387" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per-pŏpŭlor</span></b> ,
			ātus, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. dep. a.</i>, <i>to lay
				quite waste</i>, <i>ravage</i>, <i>devastate; to plunder</i> or <i>pillage
				completely</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agrum Placentinum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					34, 56</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnia loca,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					34, 28</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Italiam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 22,
					3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 14, 26</span></i>.—<i>Part. perf.</i>, in a pass. signif.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perpopulato agro,</span>”
				<i>completely laid waste</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					22, 9, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
